Insert into CTNATURE_OF_ID (NATURE_OF_ID,DESCRIPTION) values ('ID based on geography','Specimen is assumed, on the basis of known geographic ranges, to be the taxon expected at the locality where it was collected. Used commonly with endemic taxon. The specimen may or may not have been identified to species by comparing it to the other species in the genus or group. Specimen Examined: Unknown. 
Insert into CTNATURE_OF_ID (NATURE_OF_ID,DESCRIPTION) values ('ID based on molecular data','An identification made by a laboratory analysis comparing the specimen to related taxa by molecular criteria, generally DNA sequences. Specimen Examined: Unknown.');
Insert into CTNATURE_OF_ID (NATURE_OF_ID,DESCRIPTION) values ('ID to species group',null);
Insert into CTNATURE_OF_ID (NATURE_OF_ID,DESCRIPTION) values ('Id of kin','Identification is based on a specimen that is recorded as related by being a parent, child, sibling, egg of, etc. of another specimen.');
Insert into CTNATURE_OF_ID (NATURE_OF_ID,DESCRIPTION) values ('curatorial ID','An identification determined by qualified personnel assisting with collection management including collection managers, curators, trained students, staff and others who may not be experts in the group in question but have some knowledge of relevant taxonomy.  Specimen Examined: Yes.');
Insert into CTNATURE_OF_ID (NATURE_OF_ID,DESCRIPTION) values ('erroneous citation',' While entering determinations and comparing them to current determinations, errors within the publications sometimes become evident. If the author''s intention can be established with reasonable certainty, then create an additional ID and citation to the correct specimen. The actual (incorrectly) cited identification should be designated “erroneous citation” and identification remarks should include something like “An incorrect reference to MCZ:Mamm:1234 is listed in citation, the citation should reference MCZ:Mamm:5555."  Document the basis of the "reasonable certainty” in the identification remarks.   This is likely a case where extensive notes are needed on both specimens.  Specimen Examined: Yes.');
Insert into CTNATURE_OF_ID (NATURE_OF_ID,DESCRIPTION) values ('erroneous on label','Errors on the label. If you can establish the author''s intention with reasonable certainty, then create an additional ID to the correct name.  ID Remarks for the incorrect name should say something like, "the spelling "Bufo bfo" of Bufo bufo is present on a label in Smith''s hand."   The correct name SHOULD have the value curatorial ID or expert ID.  Do not use this designation to indicate an error in transcription from a label, simply fix the transcription error.  
Insert into CTNATURE_OF_ID (NATURE_OF_ID,DESCRIPTION) values ('expert ID','The determiner is a person with expertise in the taxon in question or the regional biota.  Specimen could be cited in taxonomic publication by an expert. Specimen Examined: Yes.
Insert into CTNATURE_OF_ID (NATURE_OF_ID,DESCRIPTION) values ('field ID','An initial determination made in the field without access to specialized equipment or references. ID Remarks MUST provide the basis for knowledge that this is an ID made in the field (e.g. "written on a field label in Smith''s hand") Specimen Examined: Yes.  ');
Insert into CTNATURE_OF_ID (NATURE_OF_ID,DESCRIPTION) values ('legacy','The identification was transcribed from a ledger or other historical documentation. Specimen Examined: Unknown.');
Insert into CTNATURE_OF_ID (NATURE_OF_ID,DESCRIPTION) values ('migration','The identification was migrated to MCZbase from a now archived departmental database. The origins of the identification may not be known.  The ID SHOULD be reviewed. Specimen Examined: Unknown. ');
Insert into CTNATURE_OF_ID (NATURE_OF_ID,DESCRIPTION) values ('non-expert ID','Specimen has been identified by a person using appropriate references, knowledge, and/or and tools, but not by an expert.   Specimen Examined: Yes. ');
Insert into CTNATURE_OF_ID (NATURE_OF_ID,DESCRIPTION) values ('revised taxonomy','Any taxonomic change where the specimen has not been examined or does not need to be examined to apply the new name. This designation is appropriate only in the presence of an earlier identification. It indicates that the specimen has not been reexamined, and only that a different taxonomic name is being applied to the existing name. This may result from any change in taxonomy where the specimen was not examined.  Taxonomic revisions SHOULD NOT be applied in cases of a synonomy in part, the splitting of one taxon into more than one, or any other case where examination of the specimen is necessary to determine which of several possible current names should be applied to the specimen. This designation is applied to the new name. Specimen Examined: No.');
Insert into CTNATURE_OF_ID (NATURE_OF_ID,DESCRIPTION) values ('sp. based on geog.','Use "ID based on geography" instead');
Insert into CTNATURE_OF_ID (NATURE_OF_ID,DESCRIPTION) values ('ssp. based on geog.','Use "ID based on geography" instead');
Insert into CTNATURE_OF_ID (NATURE_OF_ID,DESCRIPTION) values ('type ID','This specimen is a type specimen whose designation is governed by the ICZN principle of typification. The specimen record MUST contain a citation of the appropriate literature, and the determiner(s) MUST be among the authors of the publication. Specimen Examined: Yes.');
